<h3>Shape</h3>

<p><b>ONLY AFFECTS THE MAXIET ALGORITHM</b></p>

<p>Shape affects the shape of the Maxwellian.  The shape is only affected for 
energies greater than the peak for the first iteration.  Later iterations may change the shape at energies less that the peak energy.  For a shape=0 the 
maxwellian will fall off sharply, where as a shape=1.0 will cause the maxwellian 
to be flat and equal to the peak value above the maxwellian peak.</p> 


<p><br>


<p>Below is a sample of the code that calculates the maxwellian spectra.  The code has been chaged to make it more readable.
<pre>
spmx = The maximum of the Maxwellian Peak initialized to 1.0.
splmax(i) = The value of the maxwellian spectrum for bin i.
num_energy_bins = The total number of energy bins.
energy(i) = The average energy of bin i.


for (i=0;i &lt; num_energy_bins+1;i=i+1) {
    splmax(i)=energy(i)<sup>1.5</sup> * e<sup>(-energy(i)/temp)</sup>;
    if (splmax(i) &gt; spmx) { 
          spmx=splmax(i);
    }
    else {
        Splmax(i)=spmx<sup>shape</sup> * splmax(i)<sup>1-shape</sup>;
        if (splmax(i) < splmax(i-1)*0.01){ 
            splmax(i)=splmax(i-1)*.01;
        }
    }
}
</pre>
